  "arrangement": "the four parts of Hymns Ancient and Modern (public domain: published 1875; its music editor W. H. Monk died 1889): its tune, alto, tenor and bass, with the bass an octave lower where it rises above a beginner bass, some notes of the alto, tenor and bass changed so each part moves easily and the chords keep their thirds, the last two lines sung to the hymnal's own parts for the same music two lines before (it prints them for organ there), and breaths written in for beginners",
